type: software

title: "SE IdentityOps"
version: "0.1.0" # CUSTOM: Updated to match the current release version of the project
date-released: "2026-11-03" # CUSTOM: Updated to match the current release date of the project

authors:
  - family-names: Case
    given-names: Denise M.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6165-7389"
    affiliation: "Northwest Missouri State University, School of Computer Science and Information Systems, Maryville, MO, USA"

repository-code: "https://github.com/structural-explainability/se-identity-ops"
url: "https://github.com/structural-explainability/se-identity-ops"

license: Apache-2.0

abstract: >
  A research experiment: a small language for specifying, executing, and
  auditing identity-relevant operations under declared criteria, with a Lean 4
  statement of its semantics and a deterministic Python reference interpreter.
  It is tested on Chicago vendor records, an SBOM and PURL conversion,
  synthetic persistence controls, and three independent Package URL
  implementations. Related work, including LACE, LACE+, ASPEN, and ASPEN+, is
  documented in the repository.

keywords:
